uld say the family separation  policy was a disaster politically and  on a humanitarian basis but that was  short-lived  a lot of the future policies beyond that  that actually helped clean up the mess  down there and mitigate a lot of the  struggle  those were immediately swept aside by  team biden  leading to the current crisis that we  have and again they're actively trying  to cover it up and it's just it's  astonishing that president biden was  asked about this can you commit to  transparency  he said well yes eventually they said  when he said i don't know  how is that an acceptable answer of  course it's not  liz uh axios obtained some pictures of  border facilities from that have been  leaked to democratic  congressman henry cuellar and once that  happened i think it's pretty clear  that the media are going to get these  images one way or another and the white  house must know  it's losing control of the narrative  here and can't just say  this is you know just a small problem uh  that we are  dealing with well they let gabe go in  from nbc  and and they brought him to i mean a  model  facility yes really happening here  and and you know president trump going  back to he was  highly critical of the press but this is  where the press  shines freedom of the press get that  sunshine in there  blast in the lights and the cameras and  the action and you see what's going on  and the press will find out  and there should be respect for for them  and for anybody who's trying to get in  there and see the true story  you can't just sit there and say i'll  let you guys in when the optics look  better where we can clean things up  this is a humanitarian crisis obviously  and the press needs to be  very very hard and press and continue on  that and we have a moment of consensus  here and i think even the mainstream  media  are united that this is not acceptable  as guy put it guy benson liz claiman  great discussion thanks very much for  joining us this sunday

